				\usepackage{mathrsfs}
				\usepackage{upgreek}
				\setlength{\oddsidemargin}{-69pt}
				\begin{document}$${{{{{{{\rm{RMSE}}}}}}}}=\sqrt{\frac{1}{\mathop{\sum }\nolimits_{i}^{M}{w}_{i}}\mathop{\sum }\limits_{i}^{M}{w}_{i}{{{{{{{{\rm{RMSE}}}}}}}}}_{i}^{2}},$$\end{document}RMSE=1∑iMwi∑iMwiRMSEi2,where wi was the weight applied to the ith graph RMSE. For edgewise RMSEs, wi was set equal to the number of edges in each graph and for pairwise RMSEs wi was set equal to the number of compounds in the graph. The latter weighting was also used when computing the aggregate RMSE in the experimental survey. We note that this weighting scheme, along with the use of pairwise errors, was used in the FEP assessment by Schindler et al.56.
